  "note": "Self-written product warranties (保証書・保証規定 / limited warranty) for fictional makers and products: a home-appliance warranty card with repair terms (run as docs/manual, a card printed in the owner's manual) and a gadget limited-warranty page with numbered articles (run as legal/contract), each in a clean version and a planted one that differs only on the lines below. Each mistake names its kind, the line it is on, the text the clean line has there (clean) and the planted line has instead (planted), and the rule expected to report it on that line. The warranty length stated two ways is named for fact-conflict: in the card it is the same unit as the table's value (1年 and 2年), in the limited-warranty page another unit in another section (24か月 against 1年 and 12か月). A registration deadline before the purchase date is named for due-before-issue, which compares the date on a deadline line with the date on an earlier-date line; the purchase date and the registration deadline are not among its pairs yet. A rule that does not exist yet is named as the rule that should: period-part-exceeds-whole (a period said to be part of another, the free-repair period within the warranty period, given as longer than it). yarn planted warranties scores them; expected.json is the committed score.",
